{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>I am the man</b> – The ancients, of blessed memory, said that Jeremiah wrote this scroll; if so, he is the one saying 'I am the man,' or each Israelite may say it:" "<b>afflicted</b> – construct state, and the noun for the destruction or the exile is lacking:" "<b>He has seen</b> – in place of 'I have seen'; likewise 'and I alone remain' [1 Kings 19:10]." "<b>His wrath</b> – it refers back to 'all my enemies.' Some say it refers back to 'the anger of HaShem' [Lam. 2:3], but this is not correct in my eyes. This lamenter said that the foe afflicted him with the rod of His wrath."], :book :lamentations, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Lamentations -- Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%9E%D7%92%D7%99%D7%9C%D7%AA_%D7%90%D7%99%D7%9B%D7%94"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:07:37.838616023Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}